# A MASS FALL, READ FROM ABOVE (21_falls): the play camera never sees the sky,
# so a fall is read by what it does to the land -- its light thrown from where
# it burns, hard and pale for the breakup, the land's shadows swinging as it
# crosses -- and then, minutes on, its boom rolling in through the felt queue
# (src/core/sky/rumble.gd) with a shake as the shock goes over.
#   tools/tour.sh tours/falls_top.tour --seed=7 --place=coast --hour=23.4 --view=top --weather=clear:0 --fall=mass@23.5
wait 2
# The clock ran while the world warmed up; put it back before the fall.
hour 23.45
wait 0.5
shot 00-before
await fall_flash 20
shot 01-mass-light-on-the-land with fall_flash
await fall_coming 5
await fall_boom 200
shot 02-boom-arrives with fall_boom
